lingmo-installer (5.0.8.lingmo.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * installer: add users page and lingmo-dm display manager support.
  * settings.conf: enable users module in show and exec sequences so the
    installer collects username and password during installation.
  * displaymanager/main.py: add DMlingmodm class that writes
    /etc/lingmo-dm.conf with Session=lingmo-initial-setup for first-boot autologin.
    OOBE switches it to lingmo-wayland on completion.
  * displaymanager/displaymanager.conf: add lingmo-dm as first entry in
    displaymanagers list so it takes priority when installed.
  * users.conf: switch sudoersGroup wheel→sudo (Debian standard), replace
    defaultGroups with Debian standard groups (sudo, audio, video, cdrom,
    dip, plugdev, netdev, bluetooth), disable root password and reuse.
    Comment out autologinGroup (not needed on Debian with lingmo-dm).

 -- Lingmo OS Team <team@lingmo.org>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 08:00:00 +0800

lingmo-installer (5.0.7.lingmo.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 安装器背景跟随窗口尺寸，修复改分辨率后底部露白。
    背景与遮罩此前按 desktopSize() 固定几何，窗口尺寸与之不同时覆盖不全；
    现改为按 rect() 设置几何，并在 resizeEvent 中同步，pixmap 用
    setScaledContents 拉伸，不在 resize 时重建。

 -- Lingmo OS Team <team@lingmo.org>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:53:21 +0800

lingmo-installer (5.0.6.lingmo.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bound the installer card on both ends. The width was min(60% of the screen,
    screen-100) with no upper limit, so a 4K screen produced a 2304px wide card,
    and the height used qBound(480, content, 78% of the screen), whose lower
    bound wins on short or HiDPI-scaled screens (1024x600, or 911x512 logical at
    150%) and leaves the card covering 93-94% of the screen with the navigation
    bar at risk of falling off the bottom.
  * cardWidth() clamps to [720, min(1100, screen-80)] and cardMaxHeight() to 86%
    of the screen; the height lower bound is now min(480, maxH) so it can never
    exceed the upper bound. ensureSize() uses the same limit, so both code paths
    agree.
  * desktopSize() now uses availableGeometry() instead of geometry() so panels
    and docks are not covered.

 -- Lingmo OS Team <team@lingmo.org>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:40:08 +0800

